# and class(students$name)
```{r}
# Check the storage type
typeof(students$name)

# Check the class
class(students$name)
```
Answer:The typeof() and class() functions both return character. This means the name column stores text values such as Ana, Ben, Cid, Dex, and Eli.

# TODO: Now create a SECOND data frame called courses directly, without
# separate vectors first, using data.frame() with these columns:
# course_code = c("IS101", "IS102", "IS103")
# units = c(3, 3, 2)
# instructor = c("Dr. P. Reyes", "Dr. R. Santos", "Dr. S. Cruz")
```{r}
# Create a courses data frame
courses <- data.frame(
  course_code = c("IS101", "IS102", "IS103"),
