Question #5:Run summary() on students. Notice that the numeric column (age) and the logical column (passed) are summarized very differently from the character column (name).
Describe what kind of summary R produces for each of the three data types, and explain why a “mean” wouldn’t make sense for the name column.

Answer:The summary() function produces different results depending on the data type of each column. For the numeric age column, it shows the minimum, maximum, median, mean, and quartiles. For the logical passed column, it counts how many values are TRUE and FALSE. For the character name column, it shows the length, class, and mode. A mean would not make sense for the name column because names are text and cannot be added or divided like numbers.

